DATA DOWNLOADED AND USED AT RUNTIME
(no copy is stored in this repository)

The API's daily VPN refresh (apps/api/src/services/vpn-refresh.service.ts) and the
local script apps/api/scripts/build-vpn-dataset.ts download the lists below and
combine them into the dataset kept in the VPN_DATA KV namespace.

1. X4BNet lists_vpn
   https://github.com/X4BNet/lists_vpn
   VPN and datacenter IP ranges (output/vpn/ipv4.txt, output/datacenter/ipv4.txt,
   output/vpn/ipv6.txt). The project states that its scripts, curated inputs and
   generated lists are available under the MIT License.

   The lists are built from the IPLocate.io IP-to-ASN database:

     IP address data powered by IPLocate.io
     https://www.iplocate.io
     https://github.com/iplocate/ip-address-databases
     Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
     License (CC BY-SA 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

   If you publish a dataset built from these lists (for example the output of
   build-vpn-dataset.ts), keep this attribution and license it under CC BY-SA 4.0.

2. Tor Project bulk exit list
   https://check.torproject.org/torbulkexitlist
   IP addresses of Tor exit relays. The same exit-list data is published by Tor
   Metrics under a CC0 no-copyright declaration: https://metrics.torproject.org/

3. Apple iCloud Private Relay egress IP ranges
   https://mask-api.icloud.com/egress-ip-ranges.csv
   Published by Apple for network operators
   (https://developer.apple.com/icloud/prepare-your-network-for-icloud-private-relay/).
   Used only to remove Private Relay addresses from the VPN ranges; never stored.

The API's exchange-rate refresh (apps/api/src/services/fx-refresh.service.ts)
downloads USD exchange rates four times a day and keeps the latest validated set
in the CACHE KV namespace. Self-hosters can replace both sources (FX_RATES_URL,
FX_RATES_FALLBACK_URL).

4. fawazahmed0/exchange-api
   https://github.com/fawazahmed0/exchange-api
   Daily currency exchange rates, served from
   https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@fawazahmed0/currency-api and
   https://currency-api.pages.dev. Released under CC0 1.0 Universal
   (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/); no attribution required.

5. Frankfurter
   https://frankfurter.dev
   Exchange rates blended from central banks and official sources, used to
   cross-check the rates above and as a fallback. Frankfurter's code is MIT
   licensed (https://github.com/lineofflight/frankfurter); its blended rates are,
   in its own words, "Frankfurter's own calculation and free to use".


